# Jarvis Platform / Presentation Rule

- Jarvis Core is platform-level and must not depend on Discord transport.
- Digital Me / Discord is a client/subsystem.
- Keep SocialBrain as Discord turn-taking policy until an explicit migration task changes it.
- Brain, Persona, and Voice are independent selections.
- Voice selection alone must not load/change persona behavior.
- Persona selection alone must not change the voice model.
- Preserve legacy current behavior through compatibility adapters while migrating.
- Persona may change style, slang, humor, wording and social tone, but must not contradict verified facts/tool results.
- Presentation code must not call live tools; tool use belongs to Jarvis Core.
- Preserve persona-scoped behavior isolation and all voice consent/privacy rules.
- Do not make SQLite/Qdrant/Obsidian migration changes merely because this architecture exists.
- Prefer interfaces/adapters and tests before broad rewrites.
